From 8ed142eab8b54cf7b2d10be2f115f2269b7fac36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 05:17:01 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] [mpegts] End the last frame of a segment where the next
 PES starts

At the end of the data of a segment, the seek scan completes the last
frame. The parsers took all the data up to the end as that frame, also
the start of the next PES, and then dropped the rest of that PES in the
next segment. So when a segment ended in the first bytes of a key frame
or right after the PES header, the seek lost that key frame. The PTS of
a PES belongs to the first frame that starts in the PES, and HLS puts
each video frame in its own PES. So the last frame now ends where a
later PES with a PTS starts, and the next segment continues the next
frame.

At the end of the data, the last HEVC NAL unit can continue in the next
segment. The parser read a parameter set there as a complete parameter
set, and then did not read the rest. The parser now uses that NAL unit
only to end a frame, and reads the NAL unit again with the data of the
next segment.

The tests end the first segment at each byte of the first TS packet of
the key frame for H.264, HEVC and MPEG-2, and check the stream
information at the landing and at the end. The parser test ends the
data at each byte of a key frame.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
